{"name":"High Seas","hex":"#7dabd8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high seas","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The regions of the ocean that are far from shore, especially those regions that do not belong to any country.","The regions of the Internet in which piracy (i.e. copyright infringement) is prevalent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_seas"}],"entries":[{"title":"International waters","blocks":[{"text":"The terms international waters or transboundary waters apply where any of the following types of bodies of water transcend international boundaries: oceans, large marine ecosystems, enclosed or semi-enclosed regional seas and estuaries, rivers, lakes, groundwater systems (aquifers), and wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Exclusive_Economic_Zones.svg/330px-Exclusive_Economic_Zones.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_waters","wikidata":"Q25855"},{"title":"High Seas (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"High Seas is a Spanish mystery series released on Netflix in May 2019. The program is set aboard a transatlantic ocean liner. It stars Ivana Baquero, Alejandra Onieva, Jon Kortajarena, Eloy Azorín, Chiqui Fernández, Tamar Novas, Daniel Lundh, Natalia Rodríguez, Laura Prats, Ignacio Montes, Begoña Vargas, and Manuela Vellés. The show was renewed for a second season in June 2019 and was released on November 22, 2019. Bambú Producciones is the production company behind the series. Actor Jon Kortajarena, who portrays character Nicolás Vázquez, confirmed season three of the show on his official Instagram page on November 6, 2019. A planned fourth season was cancelled by Netflix in mid-2020."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Seas_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q59591953"},{"title":"List of seas on Earth","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of seas of the World Ocean, including marginal seas, areas of water, various gulfs, bights, bays, and straits. In many cases it is a matter of tradition for a body of water to be named a sea or a bay, etc., therefore all these types are listed here. Entities called \"seas\" which are not divisions of the World Ocean are not included in this list, nor are ocean gyres."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Oceans_and_seas_boundaries_map-en.svg/330px-Oceans_and_seas_boundaries_map-en.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_seas_on_Earth","wikidata":"Q229088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Kom%C3%A1rom114.JPG/500px-Kom%C3%A1rom114.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Kom%C3%A1rom114.JPG/1280px-Kom%C3%A1rom114.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Kom%C3%A1rom114.JPG/500px-Kom%C3%A1rom114.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Komárno, in Slovakia, is an inland port on the Danube River, which is an important international waterway.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKom%C3%A1rom114.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Clouds_over_the_Atlantic_Ocean.jpg/500px-Clouds_over_the_Atlantic_Ocean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Clouds_over_the_Atlantic_Ocean.jpg/1280px-Clouds_over_the_Atlantic_Ocean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Clouds_over_the_Atlantic_Ocean.jpg/500px-Clouds_over_the_Atlantic_Ocean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte